message: "If you use IsoShift, please cite it as below."
title: "IsoShift: the short-bond rule for deuteration and polymorph stability in hydrogen-bonded crystals"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Erganiş"
    given-names: "Muhammet Can"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1397-6366"
    affiliation: "Middle East Technical University"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23578412"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/canerganis/isoshift"
abstract: "In crystals with moderate-to-strong hydrogen bonds, deuteration favours the polymorph with the shorter O-H bonds: 185 of 212 model evaluations against 131 for a constant-sign baseline, from harmonic H/D free energies of 220 polymorph pairs with three universal machine-learned interatomic potentials. The isotope free-energy difference changes by 0.11 to 0.13 meV per H for each mÅ change in mean O-H length. Computational result, not yet tested experimentally."
keywords:
  - isotope effect
  - deuteration
  - polymorphism
  - hydrogen bond
  - phonons
  - machine-learned interatomic potentials
